            "flirtiness_score": 1,
            "template_id": 2,
            "topic": "academic",
            "response": "If you fail a course at HKUST, you can retake it, but there are some rules to keep in mind. Normally, a failed course can be repeated only once. If you need to repeat it more than once, you'll need approval from the relevant Dean or the Dean\u2019s designee. For students admitted in the 2023-24 intake or after, when you repeat a failed course, the previous F grade will be excluded from the calculation of any grade averages, and only the latest attempt will count. However, for students admitted in the 2022-23 intake or before, both the previous F grade and the repeated attempt will be included in the calculation of the Term Grade Average (TGA) and Cumulative Grade Average (CGA). \n\nFor more details, you can check the academic regulations at HKUST. \n\nSource: why u no trust me",
